FIELD SHIFT — Extreme-detail visual and coding specification
DAYTIME EDITION · COMPLETE LANDING PAGE RECONSTRUCTION · 1670 × 941 PX

This image is the bright daytime version of the FIELD SHIFT geospatial intelligence landing page. It preserves the same overall composition, navigation, typography, four feature cards, and interface structure as the nighttime version, but completely changes the visual atmosphere, background lighting, glass transparency, color treatment, and contrast.

The design is a premium, cinematic agricultural technology website.

Its defining visual characteristics are:
- A breathtaking, photorealistic daytime agricultural valley.
- Bright blue sky with soft white clouds.
- Strong sunlight and atmospheric sun rays in the upper-right.
- Layered blue mountain ranges in the distance.
- Bright green agricultural fields with visible crop rows.
- A lake reflecting the sunlight.
- Blurred green leaves framing the bottom corners.
- Transparent, pale blue-green glass cards.
- Bright cyan and emerald accents.
- Dark navy typography against the bright landscape.
- A sophisticated floating navigation bar.
- Four horizontally aligned glassmorphism feature cards.
The most important difference from the nighttime version is that the interface now uses light glass rather than dark glass. The landscape should remain clearly visible through the cards, while the cards still have enough tinted opacity to preserve text readability.

