2. Main background — daytime agricultural landscape








heimat-original.com


The background is the most important asset in the entire design.

It is not a simple image of a farm.

It is a cinematic, wide-angle landscape featuring a large agricultural valley, distant mountain ranges, a lake, and an intensely blue daytime sky.

The image should be highly detailed, realistic, and naturally illuminated.
2.1 Background composition
The photograph has several distinct depth layers.

Layer 1 — Sky

Occupies approximately the top 40–45% of the image.
- Bright azure-blue sky.
- Slightly lighter blue toward the upper-left.
- Strong blue saturation toward the upper-center.
- Pale atmospheric blue toward the horizon.
- Large soft white clouds on the left.
- More scattered white clouds on the right.
- Bright sunlight near the upper-right.
- Soft atmospheric haze around the mountain peaks.
Layer 2 — Distant mountains

Occupies approximately 35–60% of the image height.

There are multiple mountain layers.
- The farthest mountains are pale blue.
- Middle mountain ranges are medium blue.
- Foreground mountain slopes are deeper blue-green.
- The mountain silhouettes are irregular, with pointed peaks.
- Atmospheric haze reduces contrast as the mountains recede.
The tallest mountain range appears toward the right side, approximately X = 1550 px.

Layer 3 — Agricultural valley

Occupies approximately 48–75% of the image.
- Bright green fields.
- Rolling hills.
- Rows of cultivated crops.
- Small trees and hedgerows.
- Visible agricultural divisions.
- Narrow tracks and field boundaries.
- Small reflective water features.
Layer 4 — Lake

Located around the center-right of the landscape.

The lake is a relatively narrow horizontal reflective feature.

It has bright sky reflections and darker blue-green water around the surrounding vegetation.

Layer 5 — Foreground vegetation

Occupies approximately the bottom 15–25%.
- Dark green crop rows.
- Dense leaves.
- Bright green foliage.
- Out-of-focus leaves in the bottom corners.
- Stronger depth-of-field blur near the bottom-left and bottom-right.
The foreground plants frame the page and create a natural sense of depth.
