Transparency characteristics
The background must have enough transparency to reveal the scenery.

The upper portions show soft blue and green colors from the underlying landscape.

The lower portions reveal more recognizable crop rows and foliage.

The glass should diffuse the background rather than completely obscure it.

Recommended:
- Backdrop blur: 15–19 px.
- Saturation: 125–140%.
- Main background opacity: approximately 0.72–0.80.
- Border opacity: approximately 0.70–0.85.
The exact transparency must be tuned against the actual background image.

A major mistake would be setting the card background to rgba(255,255,255,0.95). That would make it look like a white opaque panel instead of the reference.
