  place-items: center;

  border-radius: 50%;

  background: rgba(195, 229, 238, 0.53);

  border: 1px solid rgba(108, 169, 190, 0.48);

  color: #29475D;

  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
}


The arrow must be centered and approximately 17 px.
9. Topographic map pattern inside cards
The feature cards contain a subtle decorative contour-line pattern.

This is a particularly important detail because it reinforces the geospatial intelligence identity.

The pattern appears around the lower areas and right-hand portions of the cards.

It resembles elevation contour lines from a geographical map.

In the daytime version, the lines are cyan, turquoise and pale blue.

They are extremely thin and partially transparent.








rivierawsfl.com


Use an SVG overlay with:
- Stroke width: 0.7–1 px.
- Opacity: 0.10–0.20.
- No solid fill.
- Smooth irregular curved paths.
- Partial clipping at the card boundaries.
Example:
.topographic-pattern {
  position: absolute;

  inset: 0;

  opacity: 0.15;

  background-image:
    url("/images/topographic-lines.svg");

  background-repeat: no-repeat;

  background-position:
    right bottom;

  background-size: 58% 100%;

  pointer-events: none;

  z-index: 0;
}


The pattern must not interfere with text readability.

It should be more visible near the lower border, where the screenshot shows delicate cyan linework.
10. Card border and lighting
The card perimeter is not a normal flat border.

It has a luminous, slightly reflective appearance.

The border is approximately 1 px.

The upper edge is brighter white-cyan.

The bottom edge is more turquoise.

The corners have soft blue-green illumination.

Recommended:
.feature-card {
  border: 1px solid rgba(103, 220, 231, 0.80);

  box-shadow:

    /* Soft external depth */
    0 5px 17px rgba(13, 104, 134, 0.13),

    /* Cyan outer glow */
    0 0 11px rgba(0, 185, 226, 0.15),

    /* Subtle green reflection */
    0 0 21px rgba(0, 211, 177, 0.08),

    /* Bright upper glass edge */
    inset 0 1px 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.85),

    /* Lower reflected light */
    inset 0 -2px 4px rgba(37, 194, 213, 0.17);
}


The glow should remain subtle.

The card must look like transparent glass illuminated by daylight, not a neon panel.

11. Bottom scroll indicator
The scroll indicator sits at the lower center of the composition.

It is positioned approximately 850–885 px from the top.

It consists of:
- Thin horizontal line extending left.
- Vertical rounded scroll icon.
- Small downward arrow.
- Text Scroll to explore.
- Thin horizontal line extending right.
The left line is approximately 300 px long.

The right line is approximately 290 px long.

The central group is approximately 140 px wide.

The icon is approximately 22 × 34 px.

The text is approximately 12 px.
Important color detail
The scroll indicator is white in the reference, despite the daytime background.

This helps it remain visible against the darker green foreground.

Use:
.scroll-indicator {
  position: absolute;

  left: 50%;
  bottom: 55px;

  transform: translateX(-50%);

  width: 770px;

  display: flex;
  align-items: center;

  gap: 25px;

  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);

  font-size: 12px;
}

.scroll-line {
  height: 1px;

  flex: 1;

  background:
    linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      transparent,
      rgba(224, 247, 255, 0.8)
    );
}

.scroll-icon {
  width: 22px;
  height: 34px;

  display: grid;
  place-items: center;

  border: 1.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.92);

  border-radius: 12px;

  color: white;
}


The icon and text should sit directly over the foreground landscape.

Do not put them inside a card.
