15. Animation and interaction specifications
The design should feel alive without being distracting.

The animations should be smooth, subtle and relatively slow.
Element	Animation	Duration
Background	Very slow parallax	20–30 seconds
Sunlight	Gentle opacity variation	8 seconds
Navigation active line	Smooth transition	250 ms
Primary CTA	Slight brightness increase	200 ms
Feature cards	Lift upward on hover	250 ms
Card borders	Gentle glow variation	3 seconds
Icon circles	Slight scale and brightness	250 ms
Scroll indicator	Gentle downward movement	1.5 seconds

Card hover effect
The cards should rise by approximately 4–5 px when hovered.

Their border becomes slightly brighter.

The background becomes marginally more opaque.
.feature-card {
  transition:
    transform 250ms ease,
    box-shadow 250ms ease,
    border-color 250ms ease,
    background 250ms ease;
}

.feature-card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-5px);

  border-color:
    rgba(0, 193, 220, 0.95);

  box-shadow:
    0 10px 24px rgba(18, 111, 144, 0.18),
    0 0 20px rgba(0, 189, 222, 0.20),
    inset 0 1px 3px rgba(255,255,255,0.95);
}


16. Responsive behaviour
The desktop composition must remain faithful to the reference.

At smaller resolutions, adjust the composition without allowing elements to overlap.
Viewport	Layout
1440 px+	Original four-card horizontal layout
1200–1439 px	Slightly smaller heading and cards
1024–1199 px	Compact navigation and four narrower cards
768–1023 px	Two-column feature grid
Below 768 px	Stacked mobile layout

At mobile sizes:
- Move the moon/sun away from the headline.
- Keep the hero left-aligned.
- Reduce the heading to approximately 43–48 px.
- Stack the four cards vertically.
- Make CTA buttons responsive.
- Keep the navigation compact.
- Preserve the bright daytime landscape.
